2. License terms
----------------

doc/copyrght.txt states that the software may be used free of charge
for private, non-commercial use by radio amateurs; that the NORD><LINK
copyright notice may not be removed from either the source or the
startup message of the compiled program; and that the terms of the
license distributed with each copy of the software apply, referring to
ALAS (doc/alas.eng, doc/alas.txt).

ALAS -- the Allgemeine Lizenz fuer Amateurfunk Software (General
Licence for Amateur Radio Software) -- permits use, copying,
modification, and distribution for non-commercial purposes, and places
duties on anyone modifying or distributing the software. Section 4.5
requires that a modifier clearly indicate their name and address and
the fact of modification, and distribute the complete source code or
provide it on demand at cost.

doc/copyrght.txt additionally states that distribution of modified
versions is permitted only with the prior consent of NORD><LINK. This
provision is in tension with the ALAS terms that the same document
directs the reader to, and which ALAS itself applies to all software
distributed under it.


