4. On obtaining consent, and on relicensing
-------------------------------------------

The consent provision in doc/copyrght.txt cannot be satisfied, because
no rights holder can be located:

  - NORD><LINK e.V. appears to be dissolved. Its website, nordlink.org,
    is no longer operating and the domain is offered for sale. No
    successor organization or contact has been identified.

  - Berndt Josef Wulf, VK5ABN, is a Silent Key.

Relicensing the work under a modern free software license such as the
GNU GPL is likewise not possible. It would require the agreement of
every rights holder listed in section 1, including a dissolved German
association and the estate of a deceased author. Furthermore, under
German copyright law (UrhG Sec. 29), copyright itself is inalienable
and cannot be transferred except by inheritance; only rights of use may
be granted, and then only by a rights holder able to grant them.

This software is therefore, in practical terms, an orphaned work. It is
maintained and distributed here in good faith, in full compliance with
the ALAS terms that doc/copyrght.txt directs the reader to, and in a
manner consistent with the evident intent of the original authors: that
this software remain freely available to radio amateurs for
non-commercial use, with its source code open and its authorship
acknowledged.

Precedent for this treatment exists within the NetBSD pkgsrc
collection, which has distributed a patched tfkiss since 2005 and
distributes other amateur radio software of similar provenance under
the license marker "generic-nonlicense" together with a restriction
against commercial use.


